  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(120.5pt, 517.27pt, " Complex heat dissipation assemblies, inferior performance, and limited flexibility are ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 531.07pt, "the primary constraints impeding the wide application and commercialization of conventional ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 544.87pt, "flexible thermoelectric devices in wearable electronics and other high-end cooling scenarios. In ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 558.67pt, "this work, we report a non-conventional design for flexible thermoelectric devices which can ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 572.47pt, "reduce the temperature to -7.03℃ at room temperature without external heat sink, achieving a ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 586.27pt, "cooling temperature drop of 29.25℃. The design is based on non-reciprocal heat transfer, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 599.95pt, "integrated with thermally conductive composites and screen-printing technologies. This approach ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 613.78pt, "takes advantage of directional heat flow, thereby eliminating the need for complex heat sink ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 627.58pt, "networks, which extend the applications of flexible thermoelectric devices from personal thermal ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 641.38pt, "management to more broader fields such as home healthcare and emergency first aid.   ")
  #line-at(96.024pt, 668.98pt, "With the rapid development of flexible electronic devices, wearable charging and cooling ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 682.78pt, "technologies have attracted increasing attention. Among various wearable electronic devices, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 696.576pt, "flexible thermoelectric devices (F-TED) possess unique advantages such as no mechanical ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 710.376pt, "components, quiet operation, and fast response ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(310.25pt, 710.376pt, "(1,2)")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(333.31pt, 710.376pt, ". They can achieve not only personalized ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 724.176pt, "cooling but also generate electricity by utilizing the temperature difference between the human ")
]

