#original-page(612pt, 792pt, (image("graphics/page-02.png", width: 163.5pt), 222pt, 581.5pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(233.81pt, 30.96pt, "Submitted Manuscript: Confidential ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#4f81bd"))
  #line-at(303.53pt, 742.416pt, "2 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 75.96pt, "body and the surrounding environment, demonstrating excellent potential in wearable cooling and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 89.78pt, "sustainable energy applications")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(223.73pt, 89.78pt, " (3-5)")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(251.45pt, 89.78pt, ".Although many progresses have been achieved in this fast ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 103.58pt, "developing field, in particular, with the introduction of 3D printing and screen printing ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(495.22pt, 103.58pt, "(6-8)")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(519.1pt, 103.58pt, ", the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 117.38pt, "structural designs, are still focused on two conventional types ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(379.27pt, 117.38pt, "(9-11)")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(409.15pt, 117.38pt, ": the vertical and lateral π-")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 131.18pt, "type structure. Both structures are vertically symmetric, leading to a bidirectional symmetry in the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 144.98pt, "internal heat flow generated by the Fourier effect ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(314.21pt, 144.98pt, "(12,13)")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(349.15pt, 144.98pt, ". The maximum cooling temperature of ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 158.78pt, "such devices can only be maintained at approximately 15-25 ℃. For power generation, the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 172.58pt, "temperature difference between the cold and hot sides of TED is usually less than 5 ℃. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 186.38pt, "Consequently, to prevent the backflow of heat flow, traditional thermoelectric devices often need ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 200.18pt, "to attach a complex and bulky structure as heat sink to the hot end to dissipate heat ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(478.9pt, 200.18pt, "(14-16)")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(514.9pt, 200.18pt, ". The ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 213.98pt, "bulky heat sink, however, considerably compromises the portability, flexibility, and reliability of ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 227.78pt, "the devices ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(128.78pt, 227.78pt, "(17,18)")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(163.7pt, 227.78pt, ". In existing research, most researchers attempt to reduce heat flow transfer by ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 241.82pt, "lowering the thermal conductivity of materials. However, the Seebeck coefficient (")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(478.66pt, 241.82pt, "𝑆")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(485.26pt, 241.82pt, "), electrical ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 255.89pt, "conductivity (")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(139.46pt, 255.89pt, "𝜎")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(146.78pt, 255.89pt, "), and thermal conductivity (")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(285.29pt, 255.89pt, "𝜅")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(292.13pt, 255.89pt, ") are strongly interdependent parameters, making it ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 269.69pt, "challenging to optimize any single one ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(260.69pt, 269.69pt, "(19)")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(280.73pt, 269.69pt, ". Reliable methods to block internal heat flow transfer ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 283.49pt, "while ensuring the unimpeded migration of carriers are still lacking at present.  ")
  #line-at(93.024pt, 297.29pt, "In this work, we propose to introduce a non-symmetrical structure to F-TED. The non-")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 311.09pt, "symmetric structure can cause non-reciprocal heat transfer through directional thermal dissipation ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 324.89pt, "(20-22)")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(107.9pt, 324.89pt, ". As it will be shown that the non-reciprocity can significantly reduce the internal energy ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 338.69pt, "loss in thermoelectric devices. The non-reciprocal heat transfer endows heat flow transfer with ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 352.49pt, "direction dependence, realizing internal heat flux blocking and significantly reducing internal ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 366.29pt, "energy loss caused by Fourier heat conduction. Without any external heat dissipation devices, this ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 380.09pt, "flexible thermoelectric device reaches a minimum cooling temperature of -7.03 ℃. This represents ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 393.89pt, "the maximum cooling performance reported to date for thermoelectric devices operating near room ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 407.69pt, "temperature ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(132.74pt, 407.69pt, "(8,23-36,38)")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(192.86pt, 407.69pt, ". Its cooling temperature difference can exceed 65 ℃, and it achieves a ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 421.49pt, "coefficient of performance (COP) of approximately 1.5 at a temperature difference of 29 ℃. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 435.31pt, "Regarding power generation, heat flux blocking can enlarge the temperature difference, enabling ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 449.11pt, "the device composed of seven units to achieve potential differences of 15.6 mV and 26.1 mV ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 462.91pt, "during human body rest and exercise states, respectively. These performance parameters are more ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 476.71pt, "competitive compared with state-of-the-art TED")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(306.65pt, 476.71pt, " (8,33-37)")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(355.27pt, 476.71pt, ". Our work demonstrates the potential ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 490.51pt, "of non-reciprocal heat transfer in improving the performance, portability, and reliability of TED, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 504.31pt, "enabling flexible TED to be used more efficiently and extensively in various cooling and energy ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 518.11pt, "recovery scenarios. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 531.91pt, "Results and discussion ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
